  "title": "Eradication of smallpox",
  "summary": "A Global Commission certified smallpox eradication at WHO headquarters in Geneva in December 1979, and the World Health Assembly certified the world free of naturally occurring smallpox in May 1980, per the CDC. The last known natural case occurred in Somalia in 1977. WHO calls it the only infectious disease to achieve this.",
